    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "but just \"being\" feels so heavy. it's like i've used up all my fuel just to get here. there's no more drive, no more purpose. everything feels so heavy and pointless now that the goal is gone. i feel like i've just completed my purpose and now i'm just... idling. isn't it strange how reaching the goal feels more like a conclusion than a beginning?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It's not strange; it's the natural consequence of building your entire self-worth on external achievements. You've been running on borrowed momentum, and now the engine is sputtering because the fuel source—the next goal—has been removed. Instead of finding a new purpose, perhaps you could find a way to simply *un-do* the striving. Let the weight settle, and see if that quiet gravity can finally carry you somewhere softer.",
